Z||000000||RICK||11-24-1999||09:40 AM||||Yesterday I was teaching my students how to use the internet.  Needing a site that they could go to, I told them to go to V8 Archies web site and to go into sales.  While I was waiting for everybody to get to the same point I started hearing some of my students say that this was an exotic Italian sports car page.  I tried not to laugh but I did get to teach them a little about our "exotic Italian sports car" that was made in the US.||||reg||7
Z||000001||dogtired||11-24-1999||02:13 PM||||Isn't teaching great!<BR>I teach Budgeting here at a local Ju Co. and always some how get to talking about cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Budgeting, cars, money, Fiero's yah they all go together.<BR>Often someone will say something about the Exotic thing I drive, when I tell them it is a pontiac I get that "deer in the headlights stare" I love it!||||reg||10
Z||000002||DJRice||11-24-1999||03:51 PM||||I was in a parking lot getting ready to load some stuff into the back of my car one day and some guy walked by and commented on my "cool car" and he just couldnt believe it when I opened the lid and there was the engine.  "Whoa, the engines in the <I>back</I>?  What kinda car is that? <B>PONTIAC</B>?  Is that really a Pontiac?<BR>I never heard of the engine in the back of a Pontiac."<P>I dont think the guy had heard of MTV either.<BR>But I did feel special, if only for just a moment.||||reg||1
